      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Decentralised agency</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Decentralised agencies are created by a specific legislative act and charged with a particular task. Some of decentralised agencies are also commonly called ‘regulatory agency’. However, there is no commonly agreed definition of the term ‘European regulatory agency’. Regulatory agencies are also referred to as ‘decentralised agencies‘, ‘traditional agencies’ or ‘satellite agencies’.</skos:definition>
